<Document lang="en" page="privacy" title="Privacy policy" description="This page explains how the zcompare app and website handle data.">
  <section>
    <h2>Local files and diagnostics</h2>
    <p>Local comparisons, editing, sessions, and reports work offline without an account. The app processes the local files you select on your Mac. By default, diagnostics do not collect file contents, full file paths, or credentials.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Sessions, recovery, and exports</h2>
    <p>Sessions and recovery copies may retain file contents, source information, review notes, or unsaved edits on your Mac. Exported reports may contain file names, source content, or thumbnails depending on the report type and content options. Check what a session or report contains before sharing it.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>SFTP connections</h2>
    <p>When you use SFTP, the app connects to the server you configure to authenticate and read files. It sends file contents to that server only when you explicitly upload them. If you choose to save a password, the app stores it in macOS Keychain. You can remove saved passwords.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Website and feedback</h2>
    <p>The website has no accounts, file uploads, or contact forms, and uses no analytics scripts or tracking cookies. The hosting provider may process request information, such as IP addresses, to serve pages.</p>
    <p>For privacy questions, use <a href="https://github.com/zwyyy456/zcompare/issues">GitHub Issues</a>. Keep personal information, private file contents, and credentials out of public issues.</p>
  </section>
</Document>
